  "agent": {
    "note": "candidate-001 feedback fixed — both were the SAME root cause (insetNode quantization at sizes that don't divide evenly). (1) ICON not centered on desktop: the glyph's insetNode margins spread the remainder INTO the tiny glyph rect, shoving it off-center/right. (2) SQUARE KPI value cut off: insetNode crushed the value BAND from 59px to 38px, so the 55px digits clipped top+bottom. FIX (per your placeRect tip): the stat-card now positions EVERY element via placeRect (exact-pixel rect + null-tile margins, which never distort the placed rect) instead of insetNode. Verified geometrically: icon dx=dy=0 + square, value font<=band at all aspects. Benefits ALL beats' rails (1-4); 9 stat-card tests pass. Mobile title clip (CHANGES BREAKDOWN) also fixed earlier. Render one-liners in .scratch/share.md.",
    "question": "Render from .scratch/share.md and check: icon centered in the chips + the Net Changes value no longer clipped (esp. square)? Good to lock Beat 4?",
    "response": {
      "body": "good. last edit is we need to reduce the height of the pie graph area. It has too much vertical space we can give to the KPI tiles beneath them so they read more easily.  the other sizes have a relatively tight bounds",
      "from": "human",
      "at": "2026-06-25T04:38:24.006Z",
